ngs"},{"surface":"கலந்த","parts":[{"text":"கலந்த","lemma":"கலந்த","gloss":"that mingled"}],"gloss":"that mingled","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"இரண்டற்கு","parts":[{"text":"இரண்டற்கு","lemma":"இரண்டற்கு","gloss":"for the two"}],"gloss":"for the two","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"என்","parts":[{"text":"என்","lemma":"என்","gloss":"my"}],"gloss":"my"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"பேதை","parts":[{"text":"பேதை","lemma":"பேதை","gloss":"foolish/innocent"}],"gloss":"innocent"},{"surface":"நெஞ்சம்","parts":[{"text":"நெஞ்சம்","lemma":"நெஞ்சம்","gloss":"heart/mind"}],"gloss":"heart"},{"surface":"பெரு","parts":[{"text":"பெரு","lemma":"பெரு","gloss":"great"}],"gloss":"great"},{"surface":"மலக்கு","parts":[{"text":"மலக்கு","lemma":"மலக்கு","gloss":"distress/agitation"}],"gloss":"distress"},{"surface":"உறுமே","parts":[{"text":"உறு","lemma":"உறு","gloss":"experience"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"உம்","gloss":"habitual suffix"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"emphatic particle"}],"gloss":"will experience indeed"}]}],"literal":"what as saying will be felt particle of doubt O friend lightning to appear / sky rising up thunders on one hand of that in response / forest peacock loudly calls out / unrelated things that mingled for the two my / innocent heart great distress will experience indeed","translation":"O friend, what will become of me? As lightning flashes, the swelling sky thunders on one hand, and in response, the forest peacock loudly calls out. Because of these two unrelated things that have joined together, my innocent heart suffers great distress!","modern":"தோழியே! மின்னல் தோன்ற, வானம் மேலெழுந்து இடி முழங்குவது ஒருபுறம்; அதற்கு எதிரொலியாகக் காட்டு மயில் உரக்கக் குரலெழுப்புவது மறுபுறம். ஒன்றோடொன்று தொடர்பில்லாத இந்த இரண்டும் ஒன்றுசேர்ந்து செய்வதால், என் பேதை நெஞ்சம் மிகுந்த கலக்கத்தை அடைகிறதே! இது என்னவென்று சொல்லப்படும்?","explanation":"The heroine speaks to her friend during the rainy season, which is the time her lover promised to return. He has not yet arrived, and the signs of the season intensify her grief. She points out that the thundering sky and the calling peacock are two unrelated elements of nature. Yet, they seem to have joined forces to torment her. This imagery belongs to the Mullai tiṇai (pastoral landscape), which deals with patient waiting, but here highlights the painful agitation of the heroine's heart. The key words are 'ஏதில' (unrelated things) and 'மலக்குறும்' (will be distressed), showing how nature's beauty can feel hostile to a lonely heart.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.77],[0.77,1.2],[1.2,1.4],[1.4,2.0],[2.0,2.9],[2.9,3.3],[3.3,3.3],[3.3,4.1],[4.1,4.46],[4.64,5.1],[5.2,5.3],[5.3,5.9],[5.9,6.8],[6.8,6.8],[6.8,7.7],[7.7,8.6],[8.6,8.9],[8.9,9.32],[9.32,9.62]],"female":[[0.0,0.53],[0.6,1.2],[1.2,1.5],[1.5,1.9],[1.9,2.1],[2.1,3.3],[3.3,3.53],[3.7,4.0],[4.0,5.0],[5.0,5.2],[5.2,5.7],[5.7,5.9],[5.9,7.2],[7.2,7.3],[7.3,7.97],[8.1,9.3],[9.3,9.7],[9.7,10.2],[10.2,10.5]]}}